# Database Best Practices

## Objective

Data layers must be correct, secure, and maintainable under growth and concurrent access.

> **If this project has no database surface:** apply the same principles to the nearest persistent equivalent (files, config, key-value stores, local caches) or skip.

## Schema and Queries

- Respect existing schema and naming; extend rather than redesign casually.
- Normalize appropriately; denormalize only with documented reason.
- Primary keys stable; foreign keys for relationships; indexes with purpose.
- Select only needed columns; filter in the store; paginate large results.
- Avoid N+1 access patterns.
- Transactions for multi-step atomic operations; keep them short.

## Safety

- Parameterized queries  -  no SQL string concatenation.
- Validate before write; constraints complement app validation.
- Versioned migrations  -  never manual prod schema edits.
- Plan backward-compatible schema evolution (`migration-safety.mdc`).

## Documentation

Update documentation in `/docs` when the change is significant (see `documentation-first.mdc`).  -  schema changes, relationships, indexing rationale.

## Cross-links

`security-first.mdc`, `performance.mdc`.

## Golden Rule

Design every data change as if the dataset will eventually be large.